Today I explored OWASP Juice Shop - a modern, intentionally vulnerable web application that taught me how contemporary applications fail despite using the latest technologies.

What I Discovered:

📌 LOGIC FLAWS - The Most Dangerous
• Purchased items for negative prices
• Applied discount coupons multiple times
• Bypassed payment workflows entirely
These exploit intended functionality, not code bugs!

📌 INSECURE AUTHENTICATION - Still a Problem
• Weak passwords on admin accounts
• Predictable session tokens
• Missing MFA on critical accounts
• Broken password reset mechanisms
81% of breaches involve compromised credentials.

📌 IMPROPER VALIDATION - The Classic Mistake
• SQL Injection through search fields
• XSS in product reviews
• API parameter manipulation
• File upload vulnerabilities
Never trust user input. EVER.

🎯Real-World Impact:
The vulnerabilities I practiced today exist in production applications:
• E-commerce platforms with price manipulation bugs
• Banking apps with authentication bypasses
• Healthcare systems with data exposure
• APIs without proper authorization

💡Key Insight:
Modern frameworks and technologies don't automatically mean secure applications. Security must be built into the design, not added as an afterthought.
